invariant: INV-7
file: handshake_message.c
catches: webpki_session_aes
builds: bin/webpki_session_aes
reason: the ClientHello writes the build's default order whatever
  ch_cfg.cipher_suites names, so a caller that probed its CPU and asked for
  another order, or left a suite out, offers what it did not ask for. The
  hello's cipher_suites bytes must be the caller's list, in its order.

--- old
    const uint16_t *suites = hs_offered_suites(cfg, &count);
--- new
    (void)cfg;
    count = SUITE_HELD_COUNT;
    const uint16_t *suites = suite_default_order;
